    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="0850" n="840" xml:id="pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.0146/219: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-29T11:00:00+07:00">October 29,
                            1943—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 29—8:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2036. Embassy is not informed in regard to discussions between Mountbatten and
                    Chiang (Department’s 1519, October 26) but will make oral inquiry of Stilwell
                    upon latter’s return from India. Stilwell is understood to have been present at
                    the conversations but so far has given us no information thereof.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
